body:
Creates `/mini-sites/cos-before/` as a reference example of poor UX patterns for cosmetic surgery clinic websites.

## Implementation

- **index.html** (143 lines): Cosmetic Surgery Clinic Y with three-column layout, rambling procedure descriptions (facelifts, rhinoplasty, liposuction, breast augmentation, tummy tuck), floating overlapping badges/stars, and flashing marquee
- **styles.css** (395 lines): White theme with intentionally chaotic design—5 mismatched nav buttons (pink/green/orange/purple/red), mixed fantasy fonts (Papyrus, Brush Script, Lucida Handwriting), absolute-positioned overlapping elements, CSS animations (bounce, spin, flash), no responsive design

## Design Anti-patterns

White background (`#ffffff`) with visual chaos: rotated elements (`transform: rotate(-2deg)`), overlapping images (`margin-left: -30px`), dashed borders, gradient promo boxes, and inconsistent typography demonstrating low engagement patterns.

```css
.floating-badge {
    position: absolute;
    top: -15px;
    right: 20px;
    transform: rotate(15deg);
    z-index: 10;
    animation: bounce 2s infinite;
}

.overlap-img {
    margin-left: -30px;
    margin-right: -20px;
    transform: rotate(-1deg);
}
```

Follows existing pattern established by `/mini-sites/derm-before/`.

